decisions:
  - id: langchain4j_adapter_boundary
    summary: LangChain4j stays behind `adapters/langchain4j`; core and application stay provider-free
  - id: deterministic_approval_boundary
    summary: model output may propose or repair but validation, scoring, promotion and rollback are deterministic
  - id: cli_first_local_shape
    summary: first system shape is a local Gradle Java CLI, not a service
  - id: sqlite_experiment_metadata
    summary: SQLite is the local metadata store through an adapter; migrations are required before adapter delivery
  - id: no_application_container_initially
    summary: container image is not applicable until distribution or remote execution is selected
  - id: jqwik_1_9_3_pending_policy_review
    summary: jqwik is pinned to 1.9.3 because jqwik 1.10.x release notes include anti-AI-agent usage language
  - id: tool_unavailable_integration_fallback
    summary: PR-less main merge is allowed only when tools are unavailable, user explicitly authorizes it, checks pass and self-review/handoff evidence is recorded

risks:
  - fake ports prove application orchestration only; real Git worktree and SQLite semantics are still deferred
  - Gradle commands need Nix daemon access in this environment; sandboxed runs can fail even when project commands pass outside the sandbox
  - model provider, workflow patch format, promotion target and fitness weights are unresolved but not blocking architecture approval
  - integration and contract commands currently report explicit not-applicable/deferred status until real adapter contracts stabilize
  - jqwik dependency should be policy-reviewed before upgrading to 1.10.x or later
  - skipping PR loses independent GitHub review and CI-before-merge; mitigated by local readiness checks, self-review and explicit user authorization

